# Tailwind + 400-line rule

## Tailwind CSS (new / updated UI)

- **Jo bhi naya UI update** ho (components, pages, layouts, feature CSS): prefer **Tailwind utility classes** in JSX/TSX.
- Do **not** grow big new plain CSS files for fresh UI work when Tailwind can cover it.
- Existing large CSS (`globals.css`, older feature CSS) — sirf touch karo jab usi change ke liye zaruri ho; whole-site Tailwind rewrite mat karo unless user bole.
- Agar Tailwind project me setup nahi hai aur UI change chahiye: **pehle Tailwind install/configure**, phir UI.
- Keep design consistent with the page you are editing (do not invent a new purple/dashboard look).

## Max 400 lines (strict)

- Source files (`app/`, `src/`, `scripts/`) **400 lines se upar mat rakho**.
- ~350+ pe split plan; edit se 400 cross hoga to **pehle split**, phir change.
- Generated dumps mat chhedo: `node_modules`, `.next`, `.next-old-*`.
- Already-over-400: next touch pe pehle split (see `max-file-lines.mdc`).
